1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:01,820
Mark 15

2
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:04,720
And as soon as it was morning,

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,780
the chief priests held a consultation

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,900
with the elders and scribes and the whole council.

5
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,720
And they bound Jesus and led him away

6
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,480
and delivered him over to Pilate.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,960
And Pilate asked him,

8
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,360
Are you the king of the Jews?

9
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,460
And he answered him,

10
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:22,400
You have said so.

11
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,580
And the chief priests accused him of many things.

12
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,400
And Pilate again asked him,

13
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,740
Have you no answer to make?

14
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,580
See how many charges they bring against you.

15
00:00:33,320 --> 00:00:35,220
But Jesus made no further answer,

16
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,080
so that Pilate was amazed.

17
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,280
Now at the feast,

18
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:42,500
he used to release for them one prisoner for whom they asked.

19
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,440
And among the rebels in prison

20
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,620
who had committed murder in the insurrection,

21
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,780
there was a man called Barabbas.

22
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,680
And the crowd came up and began to ask Pilate

23
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,200
to do as he usually did for them.

24
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:54,960
And he answered them, saying,

25
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:59,420
Do you want me to release for you the king of the Jews?

26
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,100
For he perceived that it was out of envy

27
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,160
that the chief priests had delivered him up.

28
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,840
But the chief priests stirred up the crowd

29
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,180
to have him release for them Barabbas instead.

30
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:11,500
And Pilate again said to them,

31
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,020
Then what shall I do with the man you call the king of the Jews?

32
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,160
And they cried out again,

33
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:20,320
Crucify him!

34
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:22,440
And Pilate said to them,

35
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:26,480
Woe! What evil has he done?

36
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,660
But they shouted all the more,

37
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:29,980
Crucify him!

38
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,260
Crucify him!

39
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:34,680
So Pilate, wishing to satisfy the crowd,

40
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:36,520
released for them Barabbas,

41
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,140
and having scourged Jesus,

42
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:40,300
he delivered him to be crucified.

43
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,660
And the soldiers led him away inside the palace,

44
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:45,480
that is, the governor's headquarters.

45
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:48,160
And they called together the whole battalion,

46
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,720
and they clothed him in a purple cloak,

47
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,720
and twisting together a crown of thorns,

48
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:53,960
they put it on him,

49
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,900
and they began to salute him.

50
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,900
Hail, king of the Jews!

51
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,240
And they were striking his head with a reed,

52
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:04,220
and spitting on him,

53
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:06,060
and kneeling down in homage to him.

54
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,980
And when they had mocked him,

55
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,840
they stripped him of the purple cloak,

56
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,460
and put his own clothes on him.

57
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:14,280
And they led him out to crucify him.

58
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:16,880
And they compelled a passerby,

59
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,140
Simon of Cyrene,

60
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,920
who was coming in from the country,

61
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,680
the father of Alexander and Rufus,

62
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,180
to carry his cross.

63
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,560
And they brought him to the place called Golgotha,

64
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,200
which means place of a skull.

65
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:29,860
And they offered him one of the most precious things in the world,

66
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,100
wine mixed with myrrh,

67
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,380
but he did not take it.

68
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,180
And they crucified him,

69
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:36,220
and divided his garments among them,

70
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:37,560
casting lots for them,

71
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,620
to decide what each should take.

72
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,000
And it was the third hour when they crucified him.

73
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,160
And the inscription of the charge against him read,

74
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,120
The king of the Jews.

75
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:51,040
And with him they crucified two robbers,

76
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:53,000
one on his right and one on his left.

77
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:55,520
And those who passed by derided him,

78
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:57,280
wagging their heads and saying,

79
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:58,720
Aha!

80
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:03,120
You, who would destroy the temple

81
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:05,760
and rebuild it in three days,

82
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,860
save yourself and come down from the cross.

83
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,160
So also the chief priests with the scribes

84
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,860
mocked him to one another, saying,

85
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,720
He saved others.

86
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,380
He could not save himself.

87
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:22,020
Let the Christ, the king of Israel,

88
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:24,000
come down now from the cross

89
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,200
that we may see and believe.

90
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,100
Those who were crucified with him

91
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:29,840
also replied,

92
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:33,420
And when the sixth hour had come,

93
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,780
there was darkness over the whole land

94
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:37,020
until the ninth hour.

95
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,820
And at the ninth hour,

96
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:41,000
Jesus cried with a loud voice,

97
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:57,100
Which means,

98
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,340
My God,

99
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,400
My God,

100
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:10,640
Why have you forsaken me?

101
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:14,420
And some of the bystanders hearing it said,

102
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,780
Behold, he is calling Elijah.

103
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,460
And someone ran and filled a sponge with sour wine,

104
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,420
put it on a reed and gave it to him to drink, saying,

105
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:27,700
Ah, wait, let us see whether Elijah will come to take him down.

106
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,620
And Jesus uttered a loud voice,

107
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:31,720
a loud cry and breathed his last.

108
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,820
And the curtain of the temple was torn in two

109
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:36,100
from top to bottom.

110
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:39,000
And when the centurion who stood facing him

111
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,600
saw that in this way he breathed his last,

112
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:42,340
he said,

113
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,860
Truly, this man was the Son of God.

114
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:49,740
There were also women looking on from a distance,

115
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,620
among whom were Mary Magdalene

116
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:53,980
and Mary, the mother of James the Younger

117
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,720
and of Joses, and Salome.

118
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,720
When he was in Galilee,

119
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,600
they followed him and ministered to him.

120
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:01,720
And there were also many other women

121
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:03,440
who came up with him to Jerusalem.

122
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,940
And when evening had come,

123
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,600
since it was the day of preparation,

124
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,620
that is, the day before the Sabbath,

125
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:12,680
Joseph of Arimathea,

126
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:14,520
a respected member of the council

127
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,080
who was also himself looking for the kingdom of God,

128
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,080
took courage and went to Pilate

129
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,660
and asked for the body of Jesus.

130
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:22,920
Pilate was surprised to hear

131
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,460
that he should have already died,

132
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,320
and summoning the centurion,

133
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:28,480
he asked him whether he was already dead.

134
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,280
And when he learned from the centurion

135
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,220
that he was dead,

136
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,100
he granted the corpse to Joseph.

137
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,260
And Joseph bought a linen shroud

138
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,620
and taking him down,

139
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,960
wrapped him in the linen shroud

140
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,400
and laid him in a tomb

141
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,100
that had been cut out of the rock.

142
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,540
And he rolled a stone

143
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:48,060
against the entrance of the tomb.

144
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,540
Mary Magdalene and Mary, the mother of Joses,

145
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:52,900
saw where he was laid.

